UPDATE "City" SET "intro" = 'Boston''s listings center on instruction and hosted events. Bay State Bam teaches and is home to the Troop Mahjong Boston/Worcester chapter, which hosts leagues, socials and open play. The Newton JCC runs a weekly drop-in for players who already know the basics. Mahjong Theory, South Shore Mahjong and So Bam Fun Boston also offer lessons. If you''re new, book a lesson first, then try a drop-in session.' WHERE "name" = 'Boston' AND "state" = 'MA';
UPDATE "City" SET "intro" = 'Miami''s listings include a community program and several teachers. Mahj in Miami offers beginner classes, open-play socials and private lessons, with a two-session Mahj 101 as the usual first step. The Michael-Ann Russell JCC in North Miami Beach runs a weekly Mah Jongg program with a learner-only session, and Wendy Rudman teaches private and group classes around the area. New players can start with a beginner class or a JCC learner session.' WHERE "name" = 'Miami' AND "state" = 'FL';
UPDATE "City" SET "intro" = 'San Francisco''s listings are still small but growing. The Jewish Community Center of San Francisco hosts American Mah Jongg social play and beginner classes. Toby Salk and Mahj with Molly teach around the Bay Area, and Mahjong with Kim (who also teaches online) and So Bam Fun San Francisco offer private lessons and events. If you''re new, starting with a beginner class at the JCC or booking a private lesson is the simplest way in.' WHERE "name" = 'San Francisco' AND "state" = 'CA';
UPDATE "City" SET "intro" = 'Scottsdale''s listings cover clubs, teachers and events. Phoenix Mahjong Club, despite its name, is a storefront club in Old Town Scottsdale with open play, socials, lessons and leagues. Scottsdale Mahjong Society offers open play and lessons, and North Scottsdale Mahjong Players meets at the Holland Center. Sonoran Mahjong Co. runs beginner guided open play. New players can start with a beginner lesson or a guided session.' WHERE "name" = 'Scottsdale' AND "state" = 'AZ';
